<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Here&nbsp;Be&nbsp;Crit&nbsp;/&nbsp;Opinion</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ByeBye</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Hey Nykacolaquantum,</p>
<p><strong>Nitpicks:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Webcrawler S29F87 (&quot;JUMBLE&quot;) is to search online for keywords pertaining to SCP-5042-A bi-hourly, with all results forwarded to Site-28.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The problem with using terms like &quot;bi-hourly&quot; is that it could mean twice an hour or once every two hours; I suggest clarifying.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Upon verification, Mobile Task Force Mu-50 (&quot;Not Me&quot;) is to be dispatched immediately, retrieve SCP-5042-A materials and locally disperse amnestics.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence feels a bit clanky. Also &quot;upon verification&quot; of what?</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> All the sentences in the conprocs start with &quot;are to be&quot; &quot;is to be&quot;; might want to try landing more variety.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5042 encompasses three interrelated phenomena.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As the first sentence in your description, this is fairly lackluster.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5042-A collectively refer to&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a personal opinion but it would sound better as something like, &quot;SCP-5042-A is the collective designation for&#8230;&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Recurring symbolism of eggs being broken, and/or fractures in the sky.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is both a compliment and a concern: this was the first line that actually piqued my interest.</p>
<p>So Addendum 5042-1, is probably the coolest part of this BUT I had to switch to my laptop halfway through because it's almost unreadable on mobile. It could just be my phone, but it's worth checking out because a lot of users read on mobile.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Addendum 2</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a consistency thing for me, the first addendum is 5042-1, the second should be formatted the same, 5042-2.</p>
<p>As a second note, this section feels a bit rushed– But the note at the end is well executed and brings it together nicely</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Opinion</strong><br />
So all of these nitpicks aside, and despite the beginning being a tad dry, I enjoyed this. Once this picks up it's interesting enough and has enough &quot;wtf?&quot; factor to keep me going. I think this could be refined into something great, but as is it's pretty good. +1</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
